WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.926
"Who Should Avoid Coffee?"

00:00:07.062 --> 00:00:10.080
Despite the plethora
of health-promoting benefits

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.840
associated
with drinking coffee,

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.120
including a longer life,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.640
could there be
any "grounds for concern?"

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.920
I've previously highlighted

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.840
how coffee is not for everyone.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.120
People with glaucoma

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.040
or perhaps even merely
a family history

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.000
of the eye disease

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.240
may want to stay away
from caffeinated coffee,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.160
as it can increase
pressure in the eye

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.040
and exacerbate
or contribute to glaucoma.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.080
There are case reports
of individuals with epilepsy

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.600
having dramatic decreases

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.240
in the frequency of seizures
after stopping coffee,

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.080
so avoiding it
or limiting yourself

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.600
to no more than
two and half cups (590 ml)

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.120
is certainly worth a try
if you have a seizure disorder.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.360
Coffee may also worsen
acid reflux disease.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.600
U.S.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.240
and European guidelines
for women

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.000
both suggest
reducing caffeine intake

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
to reduce symptoms
of urinary urgency

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.600
and frequency.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.560
This makes sense.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.600
Caffeine is a mild diuretic,
especially at doses found

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.520
in more than two or three cups
(480 or 720 ml) of coffee,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.480
though daily consumers
may habituate

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.760
and be less impacted.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.080
Surprisingly, though,
a meta-analysis

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.560
of observational studies
found no evidence of a link

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.280
between urinary incontinence
and coffee intake,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.280
or caffeine, more generally.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.320
In interventional studies
of caffeine reduction,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.920
half found a decrease
in urinary frequency,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.600
but for urinary incontinence,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.120
only two studies out of seven
found a significant benefit.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.800
Again, though, what's the harm
in giving it a try?

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.240
Caffeine intake
late in the day

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.240
can certainly disrupt
your sleep,

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.480
but the caffeine in four cups
(960 ml) of coffee

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.360
finished even six hours
before bedtime

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.560
can reduce total sleep time
by more than an hour,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.680
and that was
in younger individuals.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.120
Older adults' sleep

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.440
appears to be more sensitive
to caffeine.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.720
The same 400 mg of caffeine,
which is less than what's in

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.840
a venti-sized coffee
from Starbucks,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.200
cuts total sleep time

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.360
by about an hour
in young adults

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.720
(average age of 24),

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.520
but that same amount cuts off
more than two hours

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.640
among the middle-aged
(average age of 52).

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.920
What about just a single cup
(240 ml) of coffee at dinner?

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.200
It can indeed cause
a significant deterioration

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.520
in sleep quality.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.360
There are also
consistent associations

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.560
between drinking coffee

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.040
and certain adverse outcomes
during pregnancy,

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.360
including miscarriage,
early preterm birth,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.720
and low birth weight.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.800
Although coffee consumption
has not been linked

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.800
to common birth defects,

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.840
it may increase the risk
of childhood leukemia.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.600
For more on coffee
and pregnancy,

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.560
see my video
on how much is too much.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:43.040
Also, don't stick it up
your butt.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.160
A review on the questionable
safety of coffee enemas

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.840
warned against their use,

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.000
citing reports of colitis,
rectal burns, perforation,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.800
and fatal
electrolyte disturbances.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.880
Keep in mind
that daily consumption

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.480
of caffeinated beverages can
lead to physical dependence.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.720
It's no coincidence
that Americans alone

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.400
spend more than $100 billion
annually on the stuff.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.600
Caffeine withdrawal symptoms
can include days of headache,

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.360
fatigue,
difficulty concentrating,

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.040
and irritability.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.800
Ironically, coffee's tendency
to become habit-forming

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.360
could turn out to be a perk

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.456
if coffee is indeed confirmed
to slow biological aging.

